clean_summary:
Incredible advance in the treatment of pancreatic cancer. The 12-month survival rate has increased from 17% to over 50% with the new drug called daraxonrasib.

Pancreatic cancer has long been one of the least treatable cancers. This breakthrough suggests that someday all cancers may become completely curable.

@EricTopol highlights that there hasn't been a treatment for pancreatic cancer this successful before. The recent results show a doubling of survival rates, published in NEJM and presented at ASCO, with daraxonrasib, which is now available through an FDA-approved early access program and is being shipped to physicians.
